 91	\begin{proof}
 92		\leanok
 93		\uses{def:typed-cl-distributions, def:graph-distribution, def:cl-dist}
 94		Every unordered pair of types is an edge of $G^{\mathrm{ld}}$, so the graph distribution $\mu_{G^{\mathrm{ld}}}$ of Definition~\ref{def:graph-distribution} is the uniform distribution on $\mathcal T^{\mathrm{ld}} \times \mathcal T^{\mathrm{ld}}$. For each ordered type pair $(t_{\mathrm A}, t_{\mathrm B})$ the CL distribution $\mu_{L_{t_{\mathrm A}},\, L_{t_{\mathrm B}}}$ is the push-forward of the uniform distribution on $V$ along $z \mapsto \bigl(L_{t_{\mathrm A}}(z), L_{t_{\mathrm B}}(z)\bigr)$. Binding the uniform type pair to these push-forwards and tagging each content with its type is exactly the two-stage sampling procedure of Definition~\ref{def:ld-question-distribution}.
